//- Checks and quality. Params: d.
div(data-ui="prose")
  p A video can look fine on your screen and still fail on a phone: a caption under the app's buttons, a grey title on a grey photo, a word on screen too briefly to read, music that drowns the voice. The studio measures these things for you, before the render and again on the finished file.

  h2#zones Safe zones, platforms and the caption lane
  raw p("Every format has a **safe zone**, the part of the frame no platform covers. The checks use the tightest of three areas: **title-safe** (the frame minus 5 % on each side), the **format's safe zone**, and the **platform zone** of any platforms you chose.")
  div(role="region" aria-label="Format safe zones" tabindex="0")
    table
      thead
        tr
          th Format
          th Size
          th Safe zone, top / right / bottom / left
      tbody
        each f in d.live.formats
          tr
            td {{ f.label }}
            td {{ f.size }}
            td {{ f.safe }} px
  raw p("**Platform profiles** add each platform's own zones. Choose them in the clip settings (**Platforms**) or with `platforms: ['youtube', 'shorts']`. A profile applies only to the shapes it is made for: YouTube to horizontal renders, the vertical platforms to vertical renders, so one clip can carry both. Turn on **Keep assets inside the platforms' safe zone** (`safe: 'platform'`) to make assets lay out inside them.")
  div(role="region" aria-label="Platform profiles" tabindex="0")
    table
      thead
        tr
          th Profile
          th For
          th Zones at 1080p, top / right / bottom / left
          th Longest video
      tbody
        each p in d.live.platforms
          tr
            td
              strong {{ p.name }}
              |  ({{ p.id }})
            td {{ p.formats }}
            td {{ p.zones }} px
            td {{ p.maxDuration }}
  raw p("Only Meta publishes exact margins (for Reels); the other zones are careful estimates, and each profile in `src/core/platforms.js` names its sources. The **feed** profile is the union of Shorts, Reels and TikTok: use it when one vertical video goes to all three.")
  raw p("The **caption lane** is a band across the bottom of the tightest safe zone (15 % of the frame's height in vertical clips, 20 % otherwise). Captions go there and nothing else does.")

  h2#check-clip Check the clip
  raw p("Press **Check the clip** in the editor's **Issues** panel (Claude: `check_clip`). The studio draws frames every half second, measures every text the assets drew, and lists each problem with its item, its time, the numbers and a still. Click one to jump there. A problem seen on only one sampled frame of many (a text passing through) is not reported.")
  div(role="region" aria-label="What the clip check finds" tabindex="0")
    table
      thead
        tr
          th Check
          th Reported when
          th Usual fix
      tbody
        tr
          td Safe zone
          td A text box is not inside the safe zone (captions are exempt).
          td Move or shrink the item; lay it out relative to the safe zone.
        tr
          td Clipped
          td A text box goes more than a pixel past the frame's edge.
          td Give it a larger box or fewer words.
        tr
          td Overlap
          td Texts of different items overlap by more than 4 % of the smaller one.
          td Move one, or shorten the time they share.
        tr
          td Caption lane
          td A text that is not a caption sits in the caption lane.
          td Move it up, out of the band.
        tr
          td Size
          td
            raw md("A text is smaller on screen than 2.5 % of the frame's short side (or its asset's own floor).")
          td Make it larger, or use fewer words so it fits larger.
        tr
          td Contrast
          td The text's contrast against the darkest or lightest 5 % of the pixels behind it is under 4.5 : 1.
          td Put the text on a solid plate or pill, darken the background, change the colour.
        tr
          td Hold
          td
            raw md("A text is on screen for less than (its words ÷ 3) + 1 seconds: too short to read.")
          td Lengthen the item, or cut words.
        tr
          td Captions
          td A caption page breaks a rule: too many lines or characters, starting late, too short, split names or units.
          td
            raw md("Adjust the pages in the **Caption pages** panel.")
        tr
          td Glyphs
          td A character is missing from the font and would fall back to a system font (a warning for emoji).
          td Choose a font that has it, or add one.
        tr
          td First frame
          td The first frame is one flat colour.
          td Start with something on screen: a platform shows the first frame as a preview.
        tr
          td Last frame
          td The last frame is held still for less than 2 seconds.
          td End on a still picture (an end card is in within a second, then holds).
  raw p("Change the thresholds for one clip with `checks: { minTextSize: 2.5, contrast: 4.5 }`. Texts drawn with the raw canvas `fillText` are not measured: assets should draw text with `f.lib.text`.")
  +callout(variant="success")
    @content
      raw p("**Most issues have the same few fixes.** Text on a solid plate passes contrast; a text that fits at a larger size passes size; keeping titles in the middle of the safe zone avoids the platform zones and the caption lane; and ending on a still card held for two seconds satisfies the last-frame check.")

  h2#look Looking closely
  ul
    li
      raw md("The editor's **Overlays** bar draws the grid, the safe areas, the platform zones, the caption lane and the measured text boxes over the preview.")
    li
      raw md("`layout_report` lists every text in a frame with its box in frame pixels, its font, its size in the asset and on screen, its colour and its item.")
    li
      raw md("`render_clip_frame { clip, t, overlays: true }` draws one frame with the zones; `isolate: { only: [ids] }` draws some items alone.")
    li
      raw md("Check another format, a time range or an unsaved draft: `check_clip` takes `format`, `from`, `to` and a `composition`.")

  h2#render-report After the render: the render report
  raw p("Every render is measured from the encoded MP4 itself. Open **View report** on the **Renders** screen, or the **Report** in the gallery (Claude: `render_report { id, sheets: true }`).")
  div(role="region" aria-label="What the render report measures" tabindex="0")
    table
      thead
        tr
          th Measure
          th Flagged when
      tbody
        tr
          td The file
          td Not H.264 and yuv420p with BT.709 colour, AAC at 48 kHz, fast start, the exact size, frame rate, duration and frame count.
        tr
          td Loudness
          td The loudness target is missed by more than 1 LU, or the peaks are too high.
        tr
          td Black frames
          td Even a single frame is (nearly) all black.
        tr
          td Frozen picture
          td
            raw md("The picture does not change for half a second or more, outside a **hold** marker.")
        tr
          td Brightness jumps
          td
            raw md("The average brightness jumps from one frame to the next, away from a **cut** marker.")
        tr
          td Flashing
          td More than 3 flashes in any second, on the whole frame or a quarter of it: a risk for people with photosensitive epilepsy.
        tr
          td Silence
          td Sound under −50 dB for a second or more.
  raw p("The report also shows where the narration sits and **frame sheets**: one frame per second and the middle of each cut, with the times drawn in. Use **markers** to tell the studio what you meant: a **hold** where a still picture is intended, a **cut** where a scene changes.")

  h2#determinism Same input, same frames
  raw p("Because assets are pure functions, a clip draws the same pixels every time. The studio uses this: `frame_hashes` gives the SHA-256 of chosen frames, so you can prove that an old clip did not change, that a draft's frames equal the final's, or that a clip imported into another library renders identically. `npm run verify` checks pinning and determinism for the showcase.")
